usage: zc <command> [arguments] [flags]

build commands:
  build <src>          compile <src> to a native executable
  run   <src> [-- args]
                       build, then run it; args go to the program as written
  emit  <src>          emit standalone C (-o FILE, else stdout)

project:
  init [dir]           make dir (default .) a project: project.zd, and main.z when
                       it holds no unit

diagnostics:
  dump  <src>          dump the typecheck model as SQL (--canon: id-normalized)
  natives show|check|conversions|source
                       the C rows zc carries: show one, check them, print the
                       numeric rule's rows, write the generated `nativec` unit
  data <file.zd>       check a data file and print its values, defaults applied
  explain <code>       explain an error code, e.g. zc explain E0200

info:
  env                  print resolved tool paths and settings
  cobj <file.c>        build the C sources an emitted file's units need, print
                       their cached objects (and, with --link, its libraries)
  version              print the version
  help [command]       print usage, or help for one command

<src> is a unit name (hello) or a path (hello.z, ./sub/hello.z).

common flags:
  -o OUT  --src DIR  --release  --cc CC  --cc-mode MODE
  --target TRIPLE
  --cflags STR  --ldflags STR  --save-temps  --time  --fast-hash
  --readable-names  --mark-natives  --line-marks  --eager
  --system DIR  --tcc-lib DIR  -h/--help  -V/--version
A command takes its own flags only (zc help <command>). A value is
written `--name VALUE` or `--name=VALUE`.
